Architecture: aarch64
Depends: bash
Installed-Size: 3420
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @httpspycharmhelpers
Version: 1.2
Homepage: https://github.com/httpspycharmhelpers/aFakeSU
Description: VirtualSU - a userspace fake-root sandbox based on proot
 vsu is a self-contained proot-based fake su: it statically embeds proot and
 only needs the system liblog/libdl, so no proot and no root are required. It
 fakes a consistent root view (uid/gid/groups, capabilities, properties,
 SELinux labels, /proc) at the syscall layer.
 The rish/rishq bridge harvests the device's real uid/group tables through
 Shizuku; when Shizuku is absent vsu still runs, it just falls back to its
 built-in defaults. Requires the plain Termux app and aarch64.
 .
 The package installs vsu and vsud and provides neither su nor sudo, so it
 does not collide with termux-tools' su or the sudo package.
